quokka-integ: Hey CS/Eng, onboarding hit a weird behavior during a surge test. We spin up an edge proxy pool (50 containers) that each opens an outbound HTTP2 channel and does a preflight on init. At ~220 RPS we see ~30% 429s to /v1/complete. Any quick triage?

marta_cs: Thanks for the report. Are those 50 containers all hitting our endpoint at the exact same time? Also are you using ephemeral credentials or long-lived keys?

quokka-integ: They're short-lived edge containers scaled by traffic spikes, and yes they all start nearly simultaneously during the test. We use a long-lived project key for now.

dylan_eng: Sounds like a preflight stampede + connection churn. Quick mitigations: 1) avoid eager preflight on container start, 2) add randomized startup splay (0-8s), 3) enable client-side token cache so containers reuse tokens, 4) reuse HTTP2 connections with keepalive and tune max concurrent streams.

ryan_se: Also add 429 retry with exponential backoff + jitter at the request layer. Sample pseudo: ```js
async function apiCall(){
  let backoff = 100;
  for(let i=0;i<6;i++){
    const res = await client.call();
    if(res.status!==429) return res;
    await sleep(backoff + Math.random()*backoff);
    backoff = Math.min(10000, backoff*2);
  }
  throw new Error('retry-failed');
}
```And set client.Options.keepAlive = true and client.Options.maxConnections = 12.

quokka-integ: Quick change: disabled eager preflight and added 0-6s splay + keepalive + maxConnections=12. Still saw some 429s but much lower.

dylan_eng: We can also flip a tenant flag to coalesce preflight calls on our side for the next hour if you want to run bigger canaries; that'll make one backend preflight handle simultaneous requests.

marta_cs: I can request that. Do you want the coalesce flag for 2h? Also you'll want to move to ephemeral creds laterthe SDK caches ephemeral tokens better and reduces preflight cost.

quokka-integ: Yes please enable preflight coalescing for 2h while we run the test. We'll plan migrating to ephemeral creds after the canary.

signal-bot: preflight_coalesce enabled for tenant quokka-integ until ts=1809998400.

quokka-integ: After the flag and retry+splay changes, 429s are nearly gone. Sample logs: ```log
[1809991135] start: container splay=3.6s
[1809991142] preflight: cache miss -> fetched
[1809991151] complete:200 latency=140ms
```Thanks so much.

ryan_se: Great. Follow-up checklist we'll send: avoid eager prefetch; set startup_splay=0-10s; enable token cache; keepAlive=true; maxConnections tuned to your concurrency; retry(backoff+jitter). Also include instructions to request a permanent preflight quota increase if you expect many simultaneous cold boots.

dylan_eng: FYI SDK v1.5.0 improves single-flight preflight and reduces per-start cost. Ping us if you want help with the upgrade.

marta_cs: I'll add an onboarding note capturing this incident and mark account health as "onboarding-risk: mitigated" until you complete the ephemeral creds migration. Please paste a short postmortem when you're done.

quokka-integ: Will do. Appreciate the quick help :pray:
